<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY PARTICIPATION.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY PARTICIPATION.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and eight repurchase agreements it had offered in order to drain 4.835 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    352 days   20.78 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days   20.74 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     86 days   19.44 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     48 days   19.50 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     45 days   19.53 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     44 days   19.51 pct</p>
<p>    800 million     41 days   19.55 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     16 days   19.53 pct</p>
<p>    800 million	9 days   19.45 pct</p>
<p>    650 million	3 days   19.26 pct</p>
<p>    135 million	1 day    18.75 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
